you've definitely seen her somewhere or  everywhere at the age of 16 mckenna  grace has managed to make her way into  almost every single movie and tv show to  ever exist think that's an exaggeration  stay tuned to learn about the other  projects that paige from young sheldon  has been in  before mckenna was in gifted she had  already done more than a dozen  television roles including 50 episodes  of the long-running soap opera the young  and the restless  she had also taken parts in several  movies but her role in gifted is one she  may very well be typecast in a child  prodigy mckenna starred as  seven-year-old mary adler in 2017's  gifted which was filmed in 2015. she  portrayed a character who becomes the  subject of a custody battle between her  uncle frank and her grandmother evelyn  mary's mother diane died by suicide  seemingly from the stress she put  herself through obsessively trying to  solve the navier stokes problem frank  wants mary to have a chance at a normal  life fearing that a school for the  intellectually gifted could put her on a  path that would mirror her mother's but  evelyn was dedicated to seeing diane  solve the problem and wants to encourage  mary's intellect to be developed to its  full potential grace won a couple of  awards on the festival circuit for her  turn as mary she took home the 2017  awards for breakthrough performance and  best performance by a youth from the  phoenix films critics society she was  also nominated for the broadcast film  critics association's award for best  young actor and the women film critics  circle award for best young actress  in 2017 mckenna grace made the  transition from child prodigy to child  skating superstar for the dark comedy i  tonya based loosely on real life events  the film stars margot robbie as  controversial figure skater tanya  harding it tells the tale of her  formative years and the events leading  up to the january 1994 attack on fellow  figure skater nancy kerrigan an assault  in which harding's husband jeff glooly  was also implicated mckenna plays a  young tanya harding in flashback  sequences she's bullied and harassed by  her mother lavonna golden who aims to  mold tanya into a champion i tanya  explores the dysfunctional and abusive  relationships that comprise tanya's life  presenting her in a more sympathetic  light than any media coverage she'd  received in the fallout from the  kerrigan attack writer stephen rodgers  interviewed harding and glooly  separately noting that the two principal  parties had differing accounts of how  the events had unfolded during a panel  for the sag-aftra foundation rogers said  i thought well that's my way in i'll  just put everybody's point of view up  there and then let the audience decide  grace described her role as the young  harding as the most challenging role  she'd ever done because of one big  factor she had to learn to ice skate she  told the boston globe i've never done  ice skating before i'd fall and i was  all beaten up but i had to get up and  keep trying it's a sentiment that  mirrors tanya's troubled life as seen in  the film  life can change pretty quickly for kids  on a network tv drama one minute your  father is the outgoing secretary of  housing and urban development who wasn't  invited to the state of the union  address and then suddenly he's the  president of the united states that's  what happened to penny kirkman whose  father tom was chosen for the title  position on abc's political thriller  drama designated survivor when president  robert richmond addresses the nation in  front of both congress and the supreme  court an explosion rocks the capitol  building killing almost everyone inside  and leaving the country without a  working government except for tom  kirkman that is who was selected by  president richmond to not attend this  was to maintain the line of succession  so he suddenly elevated to the role of  president  sounds like a decent consolation prize  for not being invited to a party that  while memorable ended pretty badly  mckenna's role as first daughter penny  kirkman included sporadic appearances as  a recurring character rather than as a  member of the main cast she appeared in  21 of the series 53 episodes including  seven of the ten episodes in season  three which was produced and released on  netflix when abc decided not to renew  the show after season two in an  interview with red carpet news tv grace  said she enjoyed being part of her  designated survivor television family  calling kiefer sutherland and tv mom  natasha mcelhone both very very nice and  kind people she also revealed something  she has in common with her tv dad they  both have stuffed animals in their  trailers  shirley jackson's 1959 horror novel the  haunting of hill house has been directly  adapted three times twice for the big  screen in 1963 and 1999 there were the  hauntings and then there was the first  installment of netflix's the haunting  anthology series the haunting of hill  house  every incarnation of the tale involves  the supernatural goings-on at hill house  a sweeping country mansion nestled in  the hills the netflix series tells the  story of the crane family and their  experiences over the course of two  timelines 26 years apart at the spooky  location  father hugh crane has purchased hill  house and is renovating it to sell for a  tidy profit in the meantime he's moved  his wife olivia son stephen and luke and  daughters shirley theodora and nell into  the mansion  from there things go about as well as  you'd expect them to for a series with  the word haunting in the title  grace plays the young version of theo  the middle child who's arguably the most  well adjusted she also wears gloves all  the time it's not because she's a  germaphobe or something weird like that  unless of course you count having extra  sensory perception and experiencing  people's thoughts and feelings through  tactile contact is weird  living in the reality of the handmaid's  tale sounds pretty terrifying it's  reasonable to think that surviving a  coup would require some grit and  determination but then there's  witnessing the overthrow of one's  homeland at the hands of radicals who  then institute martial law and enslave  women as broodmares plus there's the  backdrop of declining human fertility  already wreaking havoc in society  dealing with all this without losing  one's mind is a huge intimidating task  thus many of the characters on the  popular hulu series have been hardened  by their experiences especially the  title handmaid june osborne it's through  this hardening that she has been able to  effectively resist and break her  shackles she rescues dozens of children  in the process via the angel's flight in  season three naturally that kind of  notoriety brings with it certain  expectations as seen through the eyes of  esther keyes the extremely young wife of  commander keys esther offers june and  the other escaped handmaid's refuge at  her farm at the beginning of the  handmaid's tale season 4. mrs keys is  strict and demanding with an insatiable  appetite for vengeance and the  devastating explanation for that is  revealed by the end of the season  premiere  grace expressed her excitement at  playing esther keys in an interview with  elle saying i thought she was so cool  she's such an interesting character to  play especially with how intimidating  she is the way she switches from being  so anxious and upset to if you weren't  going to fight then you shouldn't come  here she's angry and then she's regal  and talking to the guards she changes up  so quickly  the sitcom full house launched the  careers of many prominent child actors  including candace cameron beret jody  sweeten and twins mary-kate and ashley  olsen after that the netflix revival  show fuller house gave visibility to a  whole new generation of young talents  including mckenna grace  set in the same san francisco townhouse  as the original series and focusing on  the now grown tanner siblings as they  raise children grace appeared on eight  episodes of fuller house across four  seasons of the show her role rose heifer  pfizer harbenberger an elementary school  student and daughter of cj harbenberger  the new partner of dj's old boyfriend  steve she also starts a cute schoolyard  romance with dj's son max  i'm the king of the world  being a part of fuller house was  personally fulfilling and important to  grace as she wrote on instagram i'll  never forget sitting on the full house  couch talking with bob saget i had  watched every episode of afv and full  house and i was so excited  for a few years mckenna grace  established a small niche for herself as  the go-to young actor to play child or  tween versions of characters she  somewhat resembles in the 2019 marvel  cinematic universe entry captain marvel  the launch of brie larson's take on the  intergalactic superhero grace portrayed  carol danvers as a child in a few  sequences she also stood in for kiernan  shipka playing the child version of  sabrina spellman on an episode of  netflix's chilling adventures of sabrina  finally in the 2021 horror movie  malignant about an adult woman who was  tormented by hallucinations of horrific  murders mckenna played the kid version  of the main character portrayed by  annabelle wallace in the rest of the  film as mckenna told teen vogue i like  to make a joke that i play the younger  versions of so many people i like to say  you know if they ever do a biopic of  finn or something i'm playing the  younger version of him  she was of course talking about her  ghostbusters afterlife on-screen sibling  finn wolfhard speaking of which  potentially the biggest and most visible  project to date in the growing career of  mckenna grace is her central role in  ghostbusters afterlife the 2021 entry in  the comic sci-fi series that started way  back in 1984 with ghostbusters set more  than 30 years after the events of the  original movie ghostbusters afterlife  finds a mom moving her kids to a new  house in a new town there they learn of  their connection to the spirit-sucking  heroes who save new york more than once  starring opposite carrie [ __ ] as her  mother and finn wolfhard as her brother  is grace as young would-be ghostbuster  phoebe ghostbuster's afterlife was a 200  million dollar box office hit in the age  of covet affected theater attendants and  that was more than enough to prompt sony  to order a sequel meaning grace has  gotten herself an important role in a  major film franchise before she's even  old enough to vote  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite actors are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

